Simple vs. Present Continuous"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Present tense to talk about a routine or a specific action that happens regularly. You use the Simple Present to describe a scene, or give personal information. You can use expressions of frequency like <span class=\"italic\">every day </span> or <span class=\"italic\">always </span> with the Simple Present.<br><br>You use the Present Continuous tense to talk a current event or action happening right now. You can also use the Present Continuous to talk about events that <span class=\"strong\">are happening</span> soon.  You make the Present Continuous with the verb <span class=\"strong\"> to be + -ing</span>. You can use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">right now</span> or <span class=\"italic\">later </span>with the Present Continuous."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Simple\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The race commemorates the Maya tradition.<br><br>  I stay at home on weekends.  <br><br>I take the bus to work every morning.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The Indigenous people are commemorating their heritage today.<br> <br>I'm staying here one more night.<br> <br>We're taking the bus back to Belize City tomorrow morning.<br><br></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Past tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished event or a specific time in the past.<br>  <br>You can form the regular form of the Simple Past tense by adding <span class=\"strong\">ed</span> to the verb.<br>  <br>Some verbs are irregular. Their Past Simple form doesn't end in -ed or -ied, like <span class=\"italic\">came</span> or <span class=\"italic\">was</span>  or <span class=\"italic\">won</span>.<br>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Tense with <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ed</span> ending\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"capsize \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"capsized\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happen \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happened\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"commemorate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"commemorated \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"finish\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"finished\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past tense with irregular ending\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"come\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"came \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" lose \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lost \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"go \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"went\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"get \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"got\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"take\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"took\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "consolation prize "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a reward for the losing team "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We received the consolation prize!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in a conversation about a boat race."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "competition "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a race with a winner and a loser "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Belize River Challenge is a tough competition!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "competitive "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "enjoying competition "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't like losing. I am very competitive!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to capsize "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to flip a canoe or boat upside down "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our boat capsized a few times."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "epic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very exciting (informal) "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The competition was epic!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to com